    "short_label": {
      "en": "$bch_amt1"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "The flat monthly Child Benefit rate paid per qualifying child (children under 16, or under 19 if in full-time education/training or with a disability that prevents them supporting themselves) under Ireland's Child Benefit scheme (bch_ie). As of the latest value it is set to €140 per child per month (expressed in the raw formula as \"140#m*$sw_weeks\", i.e. the flat monthly amount scaled by the $sw_weeks constant used to convert weekly-based social-welfare figures onto the model's payment period). It is used as the per-eligible-child compensation amount (comp_perElig) in the bch_ie BenCalc function, which the func_comment notes is a monthly payment; no means test or social insurance contribution condition applies to the benefit."
    },
